  "description": "meme-id: when-youve-just-realised-your-son-has-taken-the-wrong-backpack-to-school; hasOverallIntent: harmless-comedy; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman in a hijab with a shocked expression, hands on her head, conveying exaggerated distress. The text overlays the image to describe a relatable, everyday parenting mishap — realizing a child has taken the wrong backpack to school. The scene is humorous and self-deprecating, targeting a universal parental experience. There is no toxicity present; the meme does not target any specific group based on protected characteristics, nor does it contain abusive, hateful, misogynistic, or harmful content. The intent is purely comedic, using the visual of exaggerated shock to amplify the absurdity of a minor, common parenting error. The woman’s attire is not used to stereotype or demean, but rather to represent a mother figure in a relatable context. The meme’s purpose is to evoke laughter through situational irony and exaggerated emotional reaction, not to promote harm or prejudice.",
